  "notes": "AzScan 1.14.0 - security hardening \u002B cleaner interface. Over-the-air updates are now cryptographically signed end to end: the app verifies an ECDSA signature on the update manifest AND the SHA-256 of the definitions bundle before applying anything, so a tampered or man-in-the-middle update is refused. Telemetry can only ever be sent to AzScan\u0027s own endpoint (hard-coded allowlist). Ransomware decoy (canary) filenames are now generated per install instead of being fixed, the control pipe is locked down to SYSTEM/Administrators, and the version check reads the real assembly version. Interface: the Threat Intelligence page is cleaner (internal sourcing and per-family detail moved to a dev-only view), with more breathing room and polish throughout. Keeps the full malware-category coverage, RansomShield, the Anti-Trojan ATT\u0026CK engine, IOC intelligence and the self-defense watchdog.",
